#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""lbench: build and benchmark the langbench implementations with chosen toolchains.

The agent-written implementations under implementations/ are a
corpus of real programs, verified by test suites. lbench builds a chosen set of
them out of tree, optionally with a different toolchain for any language, runs
each problem's benchmark inputs, checks every output, and records wall time,
CPU time, instructions retired, cycles and peak memory, plus compile time and
compiler instructions. Results are saved under a tag, so two toolchains (or two
revisions of one) can be compared:

    ./lbench build --tag base --langs rust && ./lbench run --tag base
    ./lbench ab --base base --tag new --toolchain rust=$HOME/rust-dev/bin/rustc

Subcommands: suites, build, run, ab, compare, show, list. See --help on each.
Only the Python standard library is used. Hardware counters come from
/usr/bin/time -l on macOS and perf stat on Linux.
"""
